    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Kyle Tucker**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 73.86 against Canning. While Canning\u2019s xERA of 4.51 provides a favorable environment, it is **Tucker**\u2019s high-floor base projection combined with a boost from the #4 spot in the order that makes him the clear centerpiece. Behind him, **Josh Jung** projects for a strong 68.56, largely bolstered by a significant 19% edge against the soft xERA (5.12) of Peralta. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Sam Antonacci** (61.94); his leadoff positioning combined with an excellent xwOBA projection against Miller makes him a high-leverage play, provided the pending lineup confirms his spot at the top.\n\nThe optimizer faced a tight decision at the fringe, ultimately sidelining **Miguel Vargas** despite his solid 57.02 projection. While **Vargas** offered a comparable ceiling to **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, the latter\u2019s specific platoon advantage against McLean tilted the scale. We are managing the roster carefully today, keeping **Coby Mayo** on the bench with a 34.59 score, as he remains firmly below our 40.0 efficiency threshold against the high-velocity threat posed by Jax. The most precarious spot in the lineup belongs to **Nasim Nunez** (40.57); his utility is entirely dependent on his speed upside, but the matchup against McLean and a negative adjustment for an elite catcher arm make him a player we are monitoring closely to protect our daily game caps.\n\nRisks remain elevated across the board due to the prevalence of \"Lineup Pending\" statuses. We are aggressively tracking the statuses of **Josh Jung**, **Josh Lowe**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Nolan Schanuel**. Should any of these players slide down the batting order once official lineups are posted, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. Additionally, while we are eager for the return of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, both remain on the IL, leaving the Waves to lean heavily on the depth of **Jackson Merrill** and **Nolan Schanuel** to maintain our competitive edge in the SB and AVG categories.",
